{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_z6zev5qvwvazqk24rfq6zvqipby2pwcyo3i6juympq6fcsj3zcyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library was\n`c_src/` is a single-translation-unit build of **stb_ds** (Sean Barrett's dynamic array + hash map library) — the `.c` half of `stb_ds.h` plus two test helpers (`strkey`, `arr_del`). The public header only declares `arr_del`, so I enumerated the real surface from the built C `.so`.\n\n## Exported ABI — 16/16 symbols, no extras\n```\narr_del              stbds_hmdel_key      stbds_hmput_key      stbds_stralloc\nstbds_arrfreef       stbds_hmfree_func    stbds_rand_seed      stbds_strreset\nstbds_arrgrowf       stbds_hmget_key      stbds_shmode_func    strkey\nstbds_hash_bytes     stbds_hmget_key_ts   stbds_hash_string    stbds_hmput_default\n```\n`nm -D` diff against the C `.so` is **empty in both directions**, for release *and* debug builds.\n\n## Files written\n`Cargo.toml` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`) and `src/{lib.rs, array.rs, hash.rs, hashmap.rs, arena.rs, tests.rs}` (1471 lines). All exports use `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"` with exact C signatures.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved (not \"fixed\")\n- **`repr(C)` layouts** for `stbds_array_header`, `stbds_hash_index`, `stbds_hash_bucket`, `stbds_string_block`, `stbds_string_arena`, plus the 64-byte `ALIGN_FWD` of bucket storage — verified identical by dumping internals.\n- **libc `realloc`/`free`/`mem*`/`str*`** rather than Rust's allocator, so allocation sizes and block ownership are interchangeable with the C version.\n- **siphash-2-4 quirks**: the seed-cancelling double XOR of `v0..v3`; C integer promotion in `data = d[0]|(d[1]<<8)|(d[2]<<16)|(d[3]<<24)` producing a *negative int that sign-extends into the upper 32 bits*; the same sign-extension in tail `case 4:`; switch fall-through semantics.\n- **`stbds_load_32_or_64` seed advance** in 32-bit-then-widened arithmetic (verified: seeds progress through identical values).\n- **Redundant `hash ^= hash ^ ROTR(...)` self-cancels** left as written; all arithmetic uses wrapping ops, and shifts use `wrapping_shl/shr` to match x86 codegen for the C's technically-UB cases.\n- `sprintf(\"test_%d\")` into a shared 256-byte static; `arr_del`'s macro expansions (`arrpush`/`arrdel`/`arrdelswap`/`arrfree`).\n\n## Verification\nI built a 19-section differential harness (compiled from the C library's own macro block, linked once per `.so`) covering hashing across lengths/alignments/seeds, array growth, int/struct/string maps in all three key modes (default/strdup/arena), tombstone rebuild and shrink paths, arena growth to the 1 MB block cap, the raw generic API, and — most tellingly — **full dumps of internal hash-index state (every bucket hash/index, seeds, thresholds, arena state)**.\n\nResult: **14894 lines byte-for-byte identical** (`cmp` clean) for both release and debug Rust builds. Along the way I also found and fixed two bugs in *my harness* (an off-by-one read past the map's last element, and unsequenced double-modification of the map pointer inside one `printf`) — the C and Rust libraries crashed at the identical instruction, which was itself corroborating evidence. `c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":155561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":432,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce35fb8d-e170-4fd3-9894-b05775c273e5","uuid":"33541b66-ec44-40f6-a37c-ed502657d32e","timestamp":"2026-08-20T02:29:37.774Z"}
